# .gitleaksignore - commit-scoped suppressions for the full history of main.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. Every gitleaks scan of this repo reads this file from the repo
# root: the scheduled full-history scan (.github/workflows/secret-scan-full-history.yml),
# CI's own secret-scan job and a local run of the same command. Each line below
# suppresses ONE finding at ONE commit. Each is a historical test fixture, canary
# or false positive; history cannot be rewritten, so these sites stay in the
# history the scan walks, and the lines keep the scan green without widening
# .gitleaks.toml.
#
# FORMAT. One fingerprint per line, exactly four parts, nothing after it:
#   <40-hex commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>
# Copy the value from the scan's own JSON report (the Fingerprint field of a
# --redact run), never by hand.
#
# TWO TRAPS, both silent:
#   1. A three-part line (file:rule:line, no commit) is a GLOBAL fingerprint. It
#      suppresses that site in every past AND FUTURE commit, so it would hide a
#      real credential committed later at the same file and line. Never write one.
#   2. Anything after the fingerprint on the same line, a trailing comment
#      included, makes the line malformed. gitleaks warns at a low level and the
#      line suppresses nothing. Comments go on their own whole lines, like these.
# src/__tests__/secret-scan-full-history.test.ts fails on both shapes.
#
# ROTATE FIRST. A finding that could be a live credential is rotated before
# anything else, and is never suppressed here. Add a line only for a fixture, and
# only after running the scan locally and reading the site:
#   gitleaks git . --config .gitleaks.toml --log-opts="--remerge-diff HEAD" --redact --no-banner
# Every group below says what kind of site it is in words and never quotes one.

